Patch BGLR 1.1.4 so its RKHS handler keeps a single retained eigenvector
column as a 1-column matrix instead of letting R drop it to a plain vector.

Without this, stock CRAN BGLR aborts with "invalid 'times' argument" on any
rank-1 kernel block — e.g. weather-GxE's weather kernel K_W built from a single
PTR weather FPC (slug wfgz1Le, weather_fpca.n_components=1). When only one
eigenvalue survives BGLR's tolD filter, `tmp` selects one column and
`LT$V[, tmp]` collapses to a vector, so the downstream outer product fails.

Applied automatically by scripts/patch_bglr.sh; see
baselines/R_HPC_SETUP.md ("Patch BGLR for rank-1 RKHS terms"). Apply with
`patch -p1 -d BGLR < baselines/bglr_rank1.patch` from a freshly untarred
BGLR_1.1.4 source tree.

--- a/R/BGLR.R
+++ b/R/BGLR.R
@@ -667,7 +667,7 @@
     tmp= LT$d > LT$tolD
     LT$levelsU = sum(tmp)
     LT$d = LT$d[tmp]
-    LT$V = LT$V[, tmp]
+    LT$V = LT$V[, tmp, drop = FALSE]

     #Default degrees of freedom and scale parameter associated with the variance component for marker effect
     if (is.null(LT$df0))
